silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_02_typed_noun_discipline_sections_03_bare_noun_cheese_trap_concrete_anchor_1_bare_cat#barenounrejected silm:hasLongDescription "The BareNounRejected is the bare singular noun 'cat' (no determiner), rejected by tau_N. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'bare_cat', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
